#
# Declarative competency questions authored as slice-resident test-DSL data,
# executed by the native Rust slice-test harness (crates/slicetest), asserted
# lane. The cells pin the questions the documentation slice exists to answer:
# which slice owns a documented term (the record→slice bridge); is every
# gmeow:DocEvidence node grounded (the fail-fast grounding invariant); is the
# maturity ladder a proper chain (Full ⊂ Maximal); does any slice CLAIM a maturity
# its coverage does not support (the HEADLINE GATE — must be empty); and which
# grounding-slice terms still lack a grounding-tier dimension (the burn-down that
# drives the grounding lift). Each runs over a self-describing gmeow:cqDataFile
# overlay scene, or the module base graph where its anchors live.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/documentation/tests/> .

# --- 1. Which slice owns a documented term? (RowsContains + overlay) ----------
# A gmeow:DocumentedTerm names exactly one owning slice; the documentation slice's
# own worked scene documents gmeow:DocEvidence, owned by the documentation slice, so
# that slice IRI is the guaranteed witness. RowsContains keeps the cell stable if the
# scene later documents further terms owned by other slices.
ex:cqDocumentedTermOwner a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQueryFile "slices/core/documentation/queries/competency/documented-term-owner.rq" ;
    gmeow:cqDataFile "examples/documented-term.ttl" ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "The documentation surface MUST be able to bridge from a term's documentation record back to the slice that owns the term: gmeow:docOwnerSlice is the record→slice edge that lets the docs group terms by slice and link a term to its slice page. Without it the documentation graph would name records with no path back to the owning vocabulary. The self-describing scene documents gmeow:DocEvidence, owned by the documentation slice, so the documentation slice IRI is the witness." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqDocumentedTermOwnerShape ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqOwnerRowDocumentation .

ex:cqDocumentedTermOwnerShape a logic:ResultShape ;
    logic:declaresColumn
        [ logic:columnVariable "owner" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ;
    logic:shapeCardinality logic:RowsContains .

ex:cqOwnerRowDocumentation a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "owner" ; gmeow:cellValueIri <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/documentation> ] .

# --- 2. Is a gmeow:DocEvidence node grounded? (ASK + overlay) -----------------
# The fail-fast grounding invariant, asked positively: the scene MUST demonstrate a
# gmeow:DocEvidence node that carries both a gmeow:docEvidenceKind and at least one
# gmeow:docGroundedBy truthmaker — the grounded discipline downstream authors copy.
ex:cqDocEvidenceGrounded a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQueryFile "slices/core/documentation/queries/competency/doc-evidence-grounded.rq" ;
    gmeow:cqDataFile "examples/documented-term.ttl" ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "Proof-carrying documentation demands that every gmeow:DocEvidence node be a claim WITH its grounds: a kind (gmeow:docEvidenceKind) and at least one carrier truthmaker (gmeow:docGroundedBy). An ungrounded evidence node is the doc-layer analogue of a DARK finding. The ASK witnesses that the worked scene holds together as a grounded evidence node." ;
    gmeow:cqExpectAsk true .

# --- 3. Is Full's intent a PROPER subset of Maximal's? (RowsContains, module base) ---
# The derived maturity lattice must place FULL strictly below MAXIMAL: the maximal
# anchor's intent must carry attributes the full anchor does not. The query returns
# the maximal-only dimensions; RowsContains pins one guaranteed witness
# (gmeow:dimAnnotationCoat, a maximal-tier dimension) so the cell stays stable as the
# ladder is extended. The anchors and their intents live in the module base graph, so
# no gmeow:cqDataFile overlay is needed.
ex:cqMaturityLattice a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQueryFile "slices/core/documentation/queries/competency/maturity-lattice.rq" ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "The named maturity anchors are distinguished intents inside the Formal-Concept lattice of the coverage incidence, and the ladder MUST be a proper chain: gmeow:docMaturityFull's intent is a strict subset of gmeow:docMaturityMaximal's. The query returns the dimensions maximal requires that full does not; a non-empty result proves Full ⊂ Maximal (proper containment), so the two tiers are genuinely distinct concepts and the maturity order is real rather than a degenerate collapse." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqMaturityLatticeShape ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqMaturityLatticeRowAnnotationCoat .

ex:cqMaturityLatticeShape a logic:ResultShape ;
    logic:declaresColumn
        [ logic:columnVariable "dim" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ;
    logic:shapeCardinality logic:RowsContains .

ex:cqMaturityLatticeRowAnnotationCoat a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "dim" ; gmeow:cellValueIri <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/dimAnnotationCoat> ] .

# --- 4. Does any slice CLAIM a maturity its coverage does not support? (RowsCount 0) ---
# The HEADLINE GATE: gmeow:sliceDocMaturity (asserted) ⊄ gmeow:docEarnedMaturity
# (projected), expressed by intent inclusion — a slice violates iff some dimension its
# claimed anchor REQUIRES is NOT among the dimensions its documentation record COVERS.
# The worked overlay carries a SUPPORTED slice (claims gmeow:docMaturityMinimal and
# covers that anchor's whole intent), so the gate holds and the query is EMPTY. The
# claim rides on the real slice IRI while the coverage rides on the gmeow:DocumentedSlice
# record, so the query bridges the two by gmeow:documents — the faithful structure over
# the regenerated bundle. cqExpectRowCount 0 pins the "no over-claim" invariant.
ex:cqMaturityNotSupported a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQueryFile "slices/core/documentation/queries/competency/maturity-not-supported.rq" ;
    gmeow:cqDataFile "tests/fixtures/maturity-projection.ttl" ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "The whole documentation standard turns on ONE gate: a slice must never CLAIM a documentation-maturity tier its coverage does not support. gmeow:sliceDocMaturity is the claim; the earned floor is the largest anchor whose intent (its gmeow:maturityRequiresDimension set) is covered. Because the anchor intents nest, asserted ⊄ earned is exactly 'some dimension the claimed anchor requires is uncovered', so the query needs no rank predicate — it reads the intent-inclusion directly off gmeow:maturityRequiresDimension and gmeow:docCoversDimension, bridging the claim (on the slice IRI) to the coverage (on the gmeow:DocumentedSlice record) via gmeow:documents. It MUST return the empty set: a non-empty result is a slice claiming a maturity it has not earned." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqMaturityNotSupportedShape ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRowCount 0 .

ex:cqMaturityNotSupportedShape a logic:ResultShape ;
    logic:declaresColumn
        [ logic:columnVariable "slice" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ;
    logic:shapeCardinality logic:RowsCount ;
    logic:shapeRowCount 0 .

# --- 5. Which grounding-slice terms lack a grounding-tier dimension? (RowsContains) ---
# The BURN-DOWN that drives the grounding lift: grounding-slice (math/logic/lang) terms
# MISSING a counter-example fixture pair, a worked instance, or a competency rationale
# (gmeow:docMissesDimension to gmeow:dimFixturePair / gmeow:dimWorkedInstance /
# gmeow:dimCompetencyRationale). Unlike the headline gate this is NOT expected empty —
# it is the work queue. The overlay demonstrates a logic-owned term missing all three,
# so the (term, dim) witness pair is guaranteed; RowsContains keeps the cell stable as
# the lift closes gaps.
ex:cqGroundingGaps a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQueryFile "slices/core/documentation/queries/competency/grounding-gaps.rq" ;
    gmeow:cqDataFile "tests/fixtures/maturity-projection.ttl" ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "A grounding slice earns its documentation maturity only when every term it owns carries the grounding-tier evidence: a counter-example fixture pair (a rule with no negative fixture is not enforced), a worked instance, and a competency question WITH a rationale. This query enumerates the exact per-term, per-dimension gaps for the three grounding slices (math, logic, lang) from the gmeow:docMissesDimension incidence, giving the grounding lift a precise, gate-derived work queue rather than an authored checklist. A non-empty result is expected while gaps remain; each closed gap drops a row." ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqGroundingGapsShape ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqGroundingGapsRowFixturePair .

ex:cqGroundingGapsShape a logic:ResultShape ;
    logic:declaresColumn
        [ logic:columnVariable "term" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ;
    logic:declaresColumn
        [ logic:columnVariable "dim" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ;
    logic:shapeCardinality logic:RowsContains .

ex:cqGroundingGapsRowFixturePair a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell
        [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "term" ; gmeow:cellValueIri <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/documentation/tests/logicTermUnderDocumented> ] ,
        [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "dim" ; gmeow:cellValueIri <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/dimFixturePair> ] .
